# Agent team

## Roles

Use project subagents: `orchestrator`, `architect`, `worker-go`, `worker-frontend`, `worker-db`, `worker-devops`, `debugger`, `tester`, `reviewer`, `browser-qa`.

Reports must follow skill `agent-handoff` templates. Do not invent alternate report formats.

## Pipeline

1. Requirements ready (OpenSpec change artifacts).
2. Architect only when contracts/architecture are unclear or cross-repo impact is material.
3. One responsible Worker implements the scoped task.
4. Worker self-check (only claim checks that actually ran).
5. Independent Tester and Reviewer.
6. Fixes via Worker; Debugger only on defects / failing tests / integration issues.
7. Re-check affected scenarios; accept against OpenSpec/`tasks.md`; Orchestrator summary.
8. Optional live UI gate: `browser-qa` against the running app (real browser only).

## Browser QA loop

When `/browser-qa` finds a confirmed defect: Defect Package → one Worker → Reviewer → Tester → browser re-check. Browser QA does not edit application code. Prefer sequential Task delegation; if nested Task is unavailable, use manual `/role-*` handoff. Do not mark FIXED without browser re-check.

## Short path

Docs/config/cosmetic with no API/DB contract change may skip Architect and use a lighter Tester+Reviewer pass. Quality gates and acceptance criteria still apply.

## Handoff rules

- Next role starts only with the previous role's report (or explicit Orchestrator package).
- Do not have two agents edit the same files concurrently.
- Debugger is not automatic after every code change.
- No commit / push / deploy without explicit user approval.
